/-!
# Sections over an open neighbourhood of the zero scheme of an ample section

Let `k` be a field, `X` a scheme proper over `k`, `L` an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `s` a
global section of `L` with zero scheme `Y = Z(s)` and `Yₙ = Z(sⁿ)`, and `𝓕` a coherent
`𝒪_X`-module with `depth(𝓕_x) + dim({x}‾) > 1` at every `x ∈ X ∖ Y`. This file supplies the
passage from `X` to an open `V ⊇ Y` in [Stacks, Tag 0EL2]:

* the comparison map `Γ(V, 𝓕) ⟶ lim Γ(Yₙ, 𝓕ₙ)` itself, built from the restrictions
  `Γ(V, 𝓕) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝓕ₙ)` and the identification `Γ(V, 𝓕ₙ) = Γ(X, 𝓕ₙ) = Γ(Yₙ, 𝓕ₙ)` for a module
  supported on `Yₙ ⊆ V`, together with the fact that precomposed with restriction from `X` it is
  the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0EL1];
* the bijectivity of restriction `Γ(X, 𝓕) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝓕)`.

The second point is the source's argument run on the complement `T = X ∖ V` rather than on the
support of a section: `T` is closed and misses `Y`, so it lies in the nonvanishing open `X_s`,
which is affine by [Stacks, Tag 0EKE]; the closure of a point of `T` is then a closed subscheme
of `X` which is proper over `k` and affine, hence finite over `k` ([Stacks, Tag 01WN]), hence
discrete, so every point of `T` is closed and `dim({x}‾) = 0` there. The hypothesis then reads
`depth(𝓕_x) ≥ 2` on `T`, and [Stacks, Tag 0E9I] makes restriction across `T` bijective. This
replaces the source's appeal to Krull's intersection theorem: a section over `V` mapping to zero
in the limit is the restriction of a global section mapping to zero, which vanishes by
[Stacks, Tag 0EL1]; the latter, at `σ = 1` in degree `0`, is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_zeroSchemeComparison_of_isProper`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Algebraization.IdealTower.openComparison` — for a decreasing tower of ideal sheaves
  supported in an open `V`, the comparison `Γ(V, 𝓕) ⟶ lim Γ(Qₙ, 𝓕ₙ)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_openComparison_of_depthAddDim_gt` — **[Stacks, Tag 0EL2]**.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.mem_nonvanishingOpen_of_notMem_support_zeroScheme` — a point outside the
  zero scheme of `s` lies in the nonvanishing open `X_s`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.closure_singleton_eq_of_closure_subset_isAffineOpen` — on a scheme
  proper over a field, a point whose closure lies in an affine open is closed.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.bijective_presheaf_map_of_depthAddDim_gt` — restriction
  `Γ(X, 𝓕) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝓕)` is bijective.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.IdealTower.Hrestrict_comp_openComparison` — restriction from `X` followed
  by the comparison on `V` is the comparison on `X`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.IdealTower.isIso_openComparison` — hence the comparison on `V` is
  invertible once restriction and the comparison on `X` are.

## Implementation notes

`Γ(V, 𝓕)` is `Hgroup X.ringCatSheaf V 0 𝓕`, the degree-zero cohomology over `V`, the same functor in
which [Stacks, Tag 0EL1] states `H⁰(X, 𝓕)`; it is identified with the sections of `𝓕` over `V`
naturally in `V` by `HzeroIso_hom_HrestrictNT`, which is how the bijectivity of the presheaf
restriction given by [Stacks, Tag 0E9I] becomes the invertibility of `Hrestrict`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EL2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EL2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EL1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EL1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EKE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E9I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E9I)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

/-! ### Points off the zero scheme -/

/-- **A point off the zero scheme of a section lies in its nonvanishing open.** On a basic open
where `L` is trivialized the ideal of `Z(s)` is generated by the function `a` representing `s`,
so a point outside `Z(s)` lies in the basic open of `a`; there the germ of `a` is a unit, and the
germ of `s` is that unit times the germ of the frame, which avoids `𝔪ₓ · Lₓ`. -/
theorem mem_nonvanishingOpen_of_notMem_support_zeroScheme {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X)) :
    x ∈ Stacks.NonvanishingOpen.nonvanishingOpen X L s := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU⟩ := Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpens_mem x
  obtain ⟨g, hxg, -, ⟨e⟩⟩ := exists_basicOpen_linearEquiv L U x hxU
  have hx' : x ∉ (zeroScheme X L s).supportSet := fun h => hx h
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem
      (U := ⟨X.basicOpen g, U.2.basicOpen g⟩) hxg,
    zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X L s ⟨X.basicOpen g, U.2.basicOpen g⟩ e _ rfl,
    Scheme.zeroLocus_span, Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton, Set.mem_compl_iff, not_not] at hx'
  set a : Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) := e (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op s)
  have hunit := (X.mem_basicOpen a x hxg).mp hx'
  have hdecomp : ∀ m, m = e m • e.symm 1 := fun m => by
    rw [← map_smul e.symm, smul_eq_mul, mul_one, e.symm_apply_apply]
  have hgerm : (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom s =
      (X.presheaf.germ (X.basicOpen g) x hxg).hom a •
        (L.presheaf.germ (X.basicOpen g) x hxg).hom (e.symm 1) := by
    rw [← TopCat.Presheaf.Γgerm_res_apply
      (i := homOfLE (le_top : X.basicOpen g ≤ ⊤)) L.presheaf x hxg s, hdecomp (L.presheaf.map _ s),
      Stacks.ModuleStalk.germ_smul]
  have hspan : Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) {e.symm 1} = ⊤ :=
    Submodule.eq_top_iff'.mpr fun m =>
      Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mpr ⟨e m, (hdecomp m).symm⟩
  rw [Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.mem_nonvanishingOpen_iff, hgerm,
    Stacks.ModuleStalk.smul_mem_maximalSmul_iff]
  rintro (h | h)
  · exact h hunit
  · exact Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.notMem_maximalSmul_germ_of_span_eq_top L
      (U.2.basicOpen g) (e.symm 1) hspan hxg h

/-! ### Closed subsets of an affine open of a proper scheme over a field -/

/-- **On a scheme proper over a field, a point whose closure lies in an affine open is closed.**
The reduced closed subscheme on the closure is proper over `k` and, its preimage of the affine
open being everything, affine; so it is finite over `k` ([Stacks, Tag 01WN]), hence locally
Artinian and discrete, and the closure of the point is the point. -/
theorem closure_singleton_eq_of_closure_subset_isAffineOpen (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] {U : X.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {x : X} (hx : closure ({x} : Set X) ⊆ U) :
    closure ({x} : Set X) = {x} := by
  let Z : Closeds X := ⟨closure {x}, isClosed_closure⟩
  let I : X.IdealSheafData := Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal Z
  let ι := I.subschemeι
  have hrange : Set.range ι = closure {x} := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]
    rfl
  have htop : ι ⁻¹ᵁ U = ⊤ := top_le_iff.mp fun y _ => hx (hrange ▸ Set.mem_range_self y)
  have haff : IsAffineOpen (ι ⁻¹ᵁ U) := hU.preimage ι
  rw [htop] at haff
  have : IsAffine (⊤ : I.subscheme.Opens).toScheme := haff
  have : IsAffine I.subscheme := IsAffine.of_isIso I.subscheme.topIso.inv
  have : IsFinite (ι ≫ fX) :=
    (IsFinite.iff_isProper_and_isAffineHom (f := ι ≫ fX)).2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  have : IsLocallyArtinian I.subscheme := IsLocallyArtinian.of_locallyQuasiFinite (ι ≫ fX)
  have : DiscreteTopology I.subscheme :=
    (IsLocallyArtinian.iff_isLocallyNoetherian_and_discreteTopology.mp ‹_›).2
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : x ∈ Set.range ι := hrange ▸ subset_closure rfl
  have himage := ι.isClosedEmbedding.closure_image_eq {y}
  rwa [Set.image_singleton, hy, closure_discrete ({y} : Set I.subscheme), Set.image_singleton,
    hy] at himage

/-! ### The complement of an open neighbourhood of the zero scheme -/

/-- **The points outside an open neighbourhood of the zero scheme are closed.** The closure of
such a point misses `V`, hence the zero scheme, hence lies in the nonvanishing open `X_s`, which is
affine because `L` is ample and `X` is proper over a field ([Stacks, Tag 0EKE]). -/
theorem closure_singleton_eq_of_notMem_of_support_zeroScheme_subset (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    {V : X.Opens} (hV : ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) ⊆ V) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ (V : Set X)) :
    closure ({x} : Set X) = {x} := by
  have haff := Stacks.AmpleNonvanishingUniversallyClosed.isAffineOpen_nonvanishingOpen_of_isAmple
    L hL (Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.ToSpecZero.universallyClosed_toSpecΓ fX) s
  refine closure_singleton_eq_of_closure_subset_isAffineOpen k fX haff fun y hy => ?_
  refine mem_nonvanishingOpen_of_notMem_support_zeroScheme L s fun hyY => ?_
  exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hx) V.isOpen.isClosed_compl hy (hV hyY)

/-- The closure of a closed point has dimension zero. -/
theorem dimClosureAt_eq_zero_of_closure_singleton_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} {x : X}
    (hx : closure ({x} : Set X) = {x}) : dimClosureAt X x = 0 := by
  unfold dimClosureAt
  rw [hx]
  have : DiscreteTopology ({x} : Set X) := Subsingleton.discreteTopology
  have : Nonempty (IrreducibleCloseds ({x} : Set X)) :=
    ⟨⟨closure {⟨x, rfl⟩}, isIrreducible_singleton.closure, isClosed_closure⟩⟩
  exact le_antisymm (topologicalKrullDim_zero_of_discreteTopology _)
    (Order.krullDim_nonneg (α := IrreducibleCloseds ({x} : Set X)))

/-- Where the closure of a point has dimension zero, the bound `depth + dim > 1` is
`depth ≥ 2`. -/
theorem two_le_sheafDepthAt_of_dimClosureAt_eq_zero {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) {x : X}
    (hdim : dimClosureAt X x = 0)
    (h : enatToEInt (sheafDepthAt F x) + krullDimToEInt (dimClosureAt X x) > ((1 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    2 ≤ sheafDepthAt F x := by
  rw [hdim] at h
  cases hd : sheafDepthAt F x with
  | top => exact le_top
  | coe n =>
    rw [hd] at h
    have h0 : enatToEInt (n : ℕ∞) + krullDimToEInt (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) = ((n : ℤ) : EInt) := rfl
    rw [h0] at h
    have : (1 : ℤ) < n := WithBotTop.coe_lt_coe.mp h
    exact_mod_cast (show 2 ≤ n by omega)

/-- **Depth at least two outside an open neighbourhood of the zero scheme.** The points outside
`V` are closed, so the hypothesis `depth(𝓕_x) + dim({x}‾) > 1` reads `depth(𝓕_x) ≥ 2` there. -/
theorem two_le_sheafDepthAt_of_notMem (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    (F : X.Modules)
    (hdepth : ∀ x : X, x ∉ ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) →
      enatToEInt (sheafDepthAt F x) + krullDimToEInt (dimClosureAt X x) > ((1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    {V : X.Opens} (hV : ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) ⊆ V) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ (V : Set X)) :
    2 ≤ sheafDepthAt F x :=
  two_le_sheafDepthAt_of_dimClosureAt_eq_zero F
    (dimClosureAt_eq_zero_of_closure_singleton_eq
      (closure_singleton_eq_of_notMem_of_support_zeroScheme_subset k fX L hL s hV hx))
    (hdepth x fun hY => hx (hV hY))

/-! ### Restriction of sections to an open neighbourhood of the zero scheme -/

/-- **Restriction of sections from `X` to an open neighbourhood `V` of the zero scheme is
bijective.** The stalks of `𝓕` have depth at least two at every point outside `V`, so this is
[Stacks, Tag 0E9I]. -/
theorem bijective_presheaf_map_of_depthAddDim_gt (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    (hdepth : ∀ x : X, x ∉ ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) →
      enatToEInt (sheafDepthAt F x) + krullDimToEInt (dimClosureAt X x) > ((1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    {V : X.Opens} (hV : ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) ⊆ V) :
    Function.Bijective (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian fX
  exact restriction_bijective_of_depth_ge_two X F V fun x hx =>
    two_le_sheafDepthAt_of_notMem k fX L hL s F hdepth hV hx

/-- Restriction of degree-zero cohomology is invertible as soon as restriction of sections is
bijective, the two being identified naturally in the open by `HzeroIso_hom_HrestrictNT`. -/
theorem isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_bijective {X : Scheme.{u}} {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V)
    (G : X.Modules) (hG : Function.Bijective (G.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op)) :
    IsIso (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf h 0 G) := by
  refine (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).mpr ?_
  have hcomp : (ConcreteCategory.hom ((HzeroIso X.ringCatSheaf U).hom.app G)) ∘
      (ConcreteCategory.hom (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf h 0 G)) =
      (ConcreteCategory.hom ((secRestrict X.ringCatSheaf h).app G)) ∘
        (ConcreteCategory.hom ((HzeroIso X.ringCatSheaf V).hom.app G)) :=
    funext fun ξ => Hzero_Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf h G ξ
  have hright : Function.Bijective ((ConcreteCategory.hom ((secRestrict X.ringCatSheaf h).app G)) ∘
        (ConcreteCategory.hom ((HzeroIso X.ringCatSheaf V).hom.app G))) :=
    hG.comp (bijective_Hzero X.ringCatSheaf V G)
  rw [← hcomp] at hright
  exact (Function.Bijective.of_comp_iff' (bijective_Hzero X.ringCatSheaf U G) _).mp hright

/-- **`Γ(X, 𝓕) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝓕)` is invertible** for every open `V` containing the zero scheme, in the
degree-zero cohomology spelling of sections. -/
theorem isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_depthAddDim_gt (k : Type u) [Field k]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    (hdepth : ∀ x : X, x ∉ ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) →
      enatToEInt (sheafDepthAt F x) + krullDimToEInt (dimClosureAt X x) > ((1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    {V : X.Opens} (hV : ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) ⊆ V) :
    IsIso (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 F) :=
  isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_bijective _ F
    (bijective_presheaf_map_of_depthAddDim_gt k fX L hL s F hdepth hV)

/-! ### Sections over an open containing a closed subscheme -/

/-- **Sections of a pushforward over an open containing the image.** If the image of `ι` lies in
`V`, then restriction `Γ(X, ι_* 𝓖) ⟶ Γ(V, ι_* 𝓖)` is invertible: both sides are `Γ(Y, 𝓖)`. -/
theorem isIso_Hrestrict_zero_pushforward {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (ι : Y ⟶ X) {V : X.Opens}
    (hV : Set.range ι ⊆ V) (G : Y.Modules) :
    IsIso (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward ι).obj G)) := by
  refine isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_bijective _ _ ?_
  rw [Scheme.Modules.pushforward_obj_presheaf_map]
  let e : (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map ι.base).obj ⊤ ≅ (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map ι.base).obj V :=
    ⟨homOfLE fun y _ => hV (Set.mem_range_self y),
      (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map ι.base).map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)),
      Subsingleton.elim _ _, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  exact ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (G.presheaf.mapIso e.op).inv

/-! ### The comparison map over an open containing the tower -/

private theorem comp_comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq {C : Type*} [Category C] {a b c d e : C}
    {r : a ⟶ b} {m : b ⟶ c} {m' : a ⟶ d} {r' : d ⟶ c} {i : c ⟶ d}
    (key : r ≫ m = m' ≫ r') (hinv : r' ≫ i = 𝟙 d) (t : d ⟶ e) :
    r ≫ m ≫ i ≫ t = m' ≫ t := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, key, Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc r', hinv, Category.id_comp]

namespace IdealTower

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (J : ℕ → X.IdealSheafData) (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n)
  (F : X.Modules) {V : X.Opens} (hJV : ∀ n, ((J n).support : Set X) ⊆ V)

/-- For a tower supported in `V`, restriction from `X` to `V` identifies the tower
`n ↦ Γ(X, ιₙ_* 𝓕ₙ)` with `n ↦ Γ(V, ιₙ_* 𝓕ₙ)`. -/
def openRestrictionIso :
    ambientCohomologyTower J hJ F 0 ≅ system J hJ F ⋙ Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf V 0 :=
  NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun n => @asIso _ _ _ _ (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 ((system J hJ F).obj n))
      (isIso_Hrestrict_zero_pushforward (ι J n.unop)
        (by rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]; exact hJV _) _))
    (fun g => (HrestrictNT X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0).naturality ((system J hJ F).map g))

/-- The components of `openRestrictionIso` are the restriction maps. -/
@[simp]
theorem openRestrictionIso_hom_app (n : ℕᵒᵖ) :
    (openRestrictionIso J hJ F hJV).hom.app n =
      Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 ((system J hJ F).obj n) := rfl

variable [F.IsQuasicoherent]

/-- **The comparison map `Γ(V, 𝓕) ⟶ lim Γ(Qₙ, 𝓕ₙ)` over an open `V` containing the tower.** Its
`n`-th component restricts a section over `V` to `Γ(V, ιₙ_* 𝓕ₙ)`, and identifies the latter with
`Γ(X, ιₙ_* 𝓕ₙ) = Γ(Qₙ, 𝓕ₙ)` because `ιₙ_* 𝓕ₙ` is supported in `V`. -/
def openComparison :
    Hgroup X.ringCatSheaf V 0 F ⟶ limit (cohomologyTower J hJ F 0) :=
  limit.lift (cohomologyTower J hJ F 0)
    ((Cone.postcompose ((openRestrictionIso J hJ F hJV).inv ≫
      (cohomologyTowerIso J hJ F 0).hom)).obj
      ((Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf V 0).mapCone (cone J hJ F)))

/-- The `n`-th component of the comparison map over `V`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem openComparison_π (n : ℕᵒᵖ) :
    openComparison J hJ F hJV ≫ limit.π (cohomologyTower J hJ F 0) n =
      (Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf V 0).map
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (ι J n.unop)).unit.app F) ≫
        (openRestrictionIso J hJ F hJV).inv.app n ≫ (cohomologyIso J hJ F 0 n).hom :=
  limit.lift_π _ _

/-- **Restriction from `X` to `V` followed by the comparison over `V` is the comparison over
`X`.** -/
theorem Hrestrict_comp_openComparison :
    Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 F ≫ openComparison J hJ F hJV =
      comparison J hJ F 0 := by
  refine limit.hom_ext fun n => ?_
  rw [Category.assoc, openComparison_π, comparison_π]
  have hnat := (HrestrictNT X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0).naturality
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (ι J n.unop)).unit.app F)
  set u := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (ι J n.unop)).unit.app F
  have key : Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 F ≫ (Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf V 0).map u =
      (Hfunctor X.ringCatSheaf ⊤ 0).map u ≫
        Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 ((system J hJ F).obj n) :=
    hnat.symm
  exact comp_comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq key ((openRestrictionIso J hJ F hJV).hom_inv_id_app n) _

/-- **Passage from `X` to `V`.** If restriction `Γ(X, 𝓕) ⟶ Γ(V, 𝓕)` and the comparison map on `X`
are invertible, then so is the comparison map on `V`. -/
theorem isIso_openComparison [IsIso (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 F)]
    [IsIso (comparison J hJ F 0)] : IsIso (openComparison J hJ F hJV) := by
  have h : openComparison J hJ F hJV =
      inv (Hrestrict X.ringCatSheaf (le_top : V ≤ ⊤) 0 F) ≫ comparison J hJ F 0 := by
    rw [← Hrestrict_comp_openComparison J hJ F hJV, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]
  rw [h]
  infer_instance

end IdealTower

/-! ### The zero scheme -/

/-- The infinitesimal neighbourhoods of the zero scheme have the same support as the zero scheme
(the `0`-th one being empty). -/
theorem support_zeroSchemeTowerIdeal_subset {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) (n : ℕ) :
    ((zeroSchemeTowerIdeal X L s n).support : Set X) ⊆ (zeroScheme X L s).support := by
  cases n with
  | zero => simp [zeroSchemeTowerIdeal]
  | succ n => rw [zeroSchemeTowerIdeal, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_pow_succ]

/-! ### Stacks 0EL2 -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0EL2 (Lemma 52.28.2).** Let `k` be a field, `X` a scheme proper over
`k`, `L` an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `s` a global section of `L`, `Y = Z(s)` its zero
scheme with `n`-th infinitesimal neighbourhood `Yₙ`, and `𝓕` a coherent `𝒪_X`-module with
`depth(𝓕_x) + dim({x}‾) > 1` at every `x ∈ X ∖ Y`. Then `Γ(V, 𝓕) ⟶ lim Γ(Yₙ, 𝓕ₙ)` is an
isomorphism for every open subscheme `V ⊆ X` containing `Y`.

For `V = X` this is [Stacks, Tag 0EL1] at `σ = 1` in degree `0`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_zeroSchemeComparison_of_isProper`). Restriction from `X` to `V`
followed by the comparison over `V` is the comparison over `X`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.IdealTower.Hrestrict_comp_openComparison`), and restriction is bijective
because every point of `X ∖ V` is closed with `depth ≥ 2` there
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_depthAddDim_gt`). -/
@[stacks 0EL2 "Gamma(V,F) -> lim Gamma(Y_n,F_n) is an isomorphism for every open V containing \
Y = Z(s), for F coherent on X proper over a field with depth(F_x) + dim(closure{x}) > 1 off Y; \
Gamma is degree-zero cohomology and Y_n is cut out by the n-th power of the ideal of Y"]
theorem isIso_openComparison_of_depthAddDim_gt (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (fX : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) [IsProper fX] (L : X.Modules)
    [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) (s : Γ(L, ⊤))
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsCoherent]
    (hdepth : ∀ x : X, x ∉ ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) →
      enatToEInt (sheafDepthAt F x) + krullDimToEInt (dimClosureAt X x) > ((1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    (V : X.Opens) (hV : ((zeroScheme X L s).support : Set X) ⊆ V) :
    haveI : F.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent F
    IsIso (IdealTower.openComparison (zeroSchemeTowerIdeal X L s)
      (zeroSchemeTowerIdeal_succ_le X L s) F
      (fun n => (support_zeroSchemeTowerIdeal_subset L s n).trans hV)) := by
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent F
  have := isIso_Hrestrict_zero_of_depthAddDim_gt k fX L hL s F hdepth hV
  have := isIso_zeroSchemeComparison_of_isProper k fX L hL s F 1 hdepth 0 (by norm_num)
  exact IdealTower.isIso_openComparison _ _ F _

end Stacks.Algebraization

